    The day in the picture is a kind one: the pointer for Mars is half a degree out only because its two kinds of error, the rough picture and the drift, happen to cancel.
[27] (as a run of characters in the old open text: False)
    All of this supposes a keeper who gave the machine one turn each time the Sun came back to the same stars.
[28] (as a run of characters in the old open text: False)
    The year of the seasons is about twenty minutes shorter than that, and had the keeper followed the seasons instead, the planets' pointers would typically be 14° to 38° out.
[33] (as a run of characters in the old open text: False)
    So the three pointers that would be nearly as good as new are the three whose ratios the reconstruction had to restore.
